From fdd53a824cba3bd177b6b474cfd557d2bbdd82da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solution40 <72304265+Solution40@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] px5g-mbedtls: add ca and sign commands

Let a router run its own small certificate authority with mbedtls only,
for routers where OpenSSL does not fit:

  px5g ca    a CA certificate: CA:TRUE (critical), keyCertSign and
             cRLSign, optional -pathlen
  px5g sign  a certificate signed by -CA/-CAkey: a server certificate
             (default: serverAuth, needs at least one subjectAltName)
             or a client certificate (-addext extendedKeyUsage=clientAuth,
             e.g. for OpenVPN; no subjectAltName needed)

Options follow selfsigned (-newkey, -key, -days, -subj, -keyout, -out,
-der, -addext subjectAltName=/extendedKeyUsage=). selfsigned, eckey and
rsakey behave as before.

The CA key has to match the CA certificate, the CA has to be a CA that
may sign and be valid now; the validity is capped at the CA's end, the
new certificate is verified against the CA before anything is written.
New keys and certificates go to temporary files that are renamed into
place only when everything worked (keys 0600, certificates 0644).

Size: about +12 KB (aarch64 13.7 -> 25.9 KB, mipsel 12.0 -> 25.6 KB,
arm_cortex-a7 11.3 -> 23.4 KB, dynamically linked to libmbedtls 3.6).
